    "post_stream": {
      "posts": [
        {
          "id": 1946656,
          "username": "mengxianying",
          "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/f1d935/{size}.png",
          "created_at": "2026-11-21T08:40:40.512Z",
          "cooked": "<p>If a Shopify Payments payout looks different from the bank deposit, start with the payout’s transaction export and the matching bank entry. Compare the payout reference, date and currency before comparing amounts.</p>\n<p>Here’s a fictional example:</p>\n<p>Two charges: $60 and $40</p>\n<p>Partial refund: -$20</p>\n<p>Processing fees: -$3</p>\n<p>Transaction net: $77</p>\n<p>If the corresponding bank deposit is $75, there is a $2 difference to investigate. First confirm that the bank entry belongs to that payout. Then check the export for refunds, adjustments and other transaction types. Keep the original transactions intact and ask your bookkeeper how the difference should be treated.</p>\n<p>For a paper trail, retain the payout reference and date, currency, transaction CSV, matching bank entry and an explanation of any unresolved difference. Shopify explains how to export payout transactions and the Amount, Fee and Net fields here: <a href=\"https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/payments/shopify-payments/payouts/view-details\" class=\"inline-onebox\">Shopify Help Center | Viewing and exporting Shopify Payments payout details</a></p>\n<p>This example uses fictional data. Does your bookkeeper need any other detail to file each payout?</p>",
