      "summarized_text": "To reconcile a Shopify Payments payout with a bank deposit, compare the payout reference, date, and currency first, then review the transaction export for refunds, fees, adjustments, and other transaction types. The post’s fictional example shows $60 and $40 in charges, a $20 refund, and $3 in processing fees, leaving a $77 transaction net; a corresponding $75 bank deposit would leave $2 to investigate. Confirm that the bank entry matches the payout, preserve the original transactions, and ask a bookkeeper how to account for any unexplained difference. For documentation, retain the payout reference and date, currency, transaction CSV, matching bank entry, and an explanation of any unresolved discrepancy. The post links to Shopify’s guidance on exporting payout transactions and understanding the Amount, Fee, and Net fields. No actual payout discrepancy is resolved; the post ends by asking what additional information a bookkeeper needs.",
